#chrom	start	end	gene
# GRCh37 coordinates for the SAME melanoma_genes.tsv driver-gene seed list as dev_intervals.bed
# (that file is GRCh38) -- added 2026-09-01, see docs/data_sources.md §1 "Real-depth data via
# ENA's pre-aligned GRCh37 BAMs" for why this exists: ENA's PRJEB27698 submission includes
# pre-aligned, deduplicated, realigned BAMs for the real COLO829/COLO829BL sequencing runs
# (ERR2752450 tumour, ERR2752449 normal), confirmed via their own @SQ header to be aligned to
# GRCh37 (bare contig names "1".."22"/"X"/"Y"/"MT", LN:249250621 for contig 1 -- GRCh37's chr1
# length, not GRCh38's 248,956,422), not GRCh38 like the rest of this pipeline's reference/GATK
# resources. This file exists to extract real reads over the same gene panel via
# `samtools view -L` directly against those remote BAMs (no full download, no re-guessing
# coordinates), which then get converted back to FASTQ and re-aligned to GRCh38 through this
# pipeline's own Module 1-2 -- see docs/data_sources.md §1 for the full extraction commands.
#
# Resolved via Ensembl's GRCh37 ARCHIVE REST API (https://grch37.rest.ensembl.org/lookup/symbol/
# homo_sapiens/<GENE>?content-type=application/json), NOT the current (GRCh38) endpoint used for
# dev_intervals.bed -- each lookup's assembly_name was confirmed "GRCh37" before use, same
# verify-don't-guess discipline as that file. Same conversion method: Ensembl gene span (1-based
# inclusive) -> BED (0-based, half-open: bed_start = ensembl_start - 1, bed_end = ensembl_end
# unchanged) -> padded +/-2000bp both ends, same rationale as dev_intervals.bed (TERT's promoter
# sits just upstream of its high-coordinate end on the minus strand -- same caveat applies here,
# see that file's comment for detail).
#
# Sequence-name convention: bare numbers ("1", "4", ...), matching these specific remote BAMs'
# own @SQ header directly -- Ensembl's GRCh37 archive API already returns bare numbers too, so
# (unlike dev_intervals.bed, which needed a "chr" prefix added for Homo_sapiens_assembly38.fasta)
# no prefix conversion was needed here.
1	115245089	115261515	NRAS
4	55522084	55608881	KIT
5	1251261	1297184	TERT
7	140417126	140626564	BRAF
9	21965750	21997300	CDKN2A
10	89620869	89733687	PTEN
17	7563096	7592856	TP53
17	29419944	29711134	NF1
